@startuml
title SplitSmart Domain Class Model (proposed)
class UserAccount
class Group
class GroupMembership
class Expense {
 amount: BigDecimal
 currency: Currency
 status: ExpenseStatus
 submittedPolicyVersion: long
}
class ExpenseShare {
 amount: BigDecimal
 selectionOrder: int
}
class ExpenseApproval {
 decision: ApprovalDecision
 stepOrder: int
}
class ReviewPolicy {
 version: long
}
class ReviewStep {
 order: int
 reviewerRule: unresolved
}
class LedgerEntry
class Payment {
 amount: BigDecimal
 idempotencyKey: String
}
class BalanceProjection
class Receipt
class Notification
UserAccount "1" -- "0..*" GroupMembership
Group "1" -- "0..*" GroupMembership
Group "1" -- "0..*" ReviewPolicy : versioned policies
ReviewPolicy "1" *-- "1..*" ReviewStep : ordered steps
Group "1" -- "0..*" Expense
Expense "0..*" --> "1" ReviewPolicy : references/snapshots applicable version
UserAccount "1" <-- "0..*" Expense : submitter
UserAccount "1" <-- "0..*" Expense : payer
Expense "1" -- "1..*" ExpenseShare
Expense "1" -- "0..*" ExpenseApproval : decisions in this review process
ReviewStep "1" <-- "0..*" ExpenseApproval : decision for step
UserAccount "1" <-- "0..*" ExpenseApproval : reviewer
Expense "1" -- "0..1" Receipt
Expense "1" -- "0..*" LedgerEntry : only after approval
Payment "1" -- "1..*" LedgerEntry
Group "1" -- "0..*" Payment
BalanceProjection ..> LedgerEntry : rebuildable from
note bottom
Conceptual model only; not implemented schema. An expense retains its submitted
policy version when group policy changes. Reviewer eligibility, self-approval,
and policy-change treatment for pending expenses remain unresolved.
end note
@enduml
